WEBVTT

01:59.800 --> 02:03.260
20: "Mozart is the Name"

02:31.770 --> 02:33.170
Wh-What...

02:34.250 --> 02:35.880
Wh-Why?!

02:40.340 --> 02:43.710
Mozart!

02:43.710 --> 02:45.030
My tummy hurts!

02:45.030 --> 02:47.070
My tummy hurts, damn it!

02:47.070 --> 02:49.360
I love the looks on your faces.

02:50.660 --> 02:55.650
Wait, huh? Are you actually pissed off?

02:56.200 --> 02:59.040
All right, all right. I won't do it anymore.

02:59.040 --> 02:59.650
Okay?

02:59.870 --> 03:01.740
It's way too early in the morning for this!

03:01.970 --> 03:03.200
Day after day...

03:03.450 --> 03:05.580
Seriously, it's getting old.

03:05.880 --> 03:06.990
Wolf!

03:07.150 --> 03:10.080
You incarnate of evil...
Your final hour is upon you!

03:19.160 --> 03:20.660
My tummy hurts!

03:20.660 --> 03:22.010
My tummy hurts!

03:22.380 --> 03:24.490
I'm going to fart!

03:27.160 --> 03:29.690
I never thought it'd work <i>this</i> well.

03:29.690 --> 03:32.460
Everything I set up worked out.

03:32.990 --> 03:36.070
How did I come up with such
a grand plan, you ask?

03:37.410 --> 03:39.900
I'd be a fool to try to explain.

03:39.900 --> 03:48.620
For the blueprints to my pranks
exist entirely in my head!

03:49.970 --> 03:50.740
Huh?

03:50.740 --> 03:51.780
Huh?

03:52.400 --> 03:55.040
Where'd you guys go?

04:14.140 --> 04:15.730
Morning, Hasshie.

04:16.150 --> 04:17.370
Yay!

04:26.290 --> 04:27.030
My.

04:27.030 --> 04:29.450
Good morning, Beethoven-san.

04:29.450 --> 04:31.250
Morning, Kanae-kun.

04:31.250 --> 04:32.870
What a fine morning.

04:33.020 --> 04:34.800
Indeed.

04:34.800 --> 04:36.380
I wonder why.

04:36.680 --> 04:37.970
I don't know.

04:37.970 --> 04:39.180
Why could it be?

04:40.020 --> 04:44.180
It may be that when man
attains true happiness,

04:44.180 --> 04:48.510
we find such ordinary life
to be the most pleasant.

04:48.740 --> 04:50.120
That's amazing.

04:50.120 --> 04:52.240
What a beautiful theory.

04:52.240 --> 04:55.140
Come to think of it,
I haven't paid my rent yet.

04:55.140 --> 04:57.000
I'm sorry, my little kitten.

04:58.100 --> 04:59.370
Rent?

05:00.110 --> 05:03.280
What silly system is that?

05:03.280 --> 05:05.070
How generous of you.

05:05.630 --> 05:07.990
Humanity is beautiful.

05:07.990 --> 05:10.690
Humanity helps one another
out in times of need.

05:10.690 --> 05:12.580
I love humanity.

05:18.540 --> 05:20.250
Morning!

05:20.250 --> 05:22.900
Mor, mor, morning, everyone!

05:23.490 --> 05:24.320
Miracle!

05:24.320 --> 05:26.130
It's a miracle morning!

05:37.890 --> 05:39.150
There you have it.

05:39.620 --> 05:44.120
I think my plan could
grant us a very nice life.

05:44.120 --> 05:44.940
Your thoughts?

05:44.940 --> 05:47.240
Absolutely not!

05:47.490 --> 05:49.340
I got eaten by a tiger!

05:49.340 --> 05:51.110
That's not going to work.

05:51.110 --> 05:53.910
We don't have a cage here, let alone a tiger.

05:53.910 --> 05:54.540
Oh, right.

05:54.540 --> 05:55.870
That's not the point!

05:55.870 --> 05:58.370
Super Cheap!!
Tiger for sale
5,000,000
Add to favorites
Add to cart

05:56.320 --> 05:58.370
A tiger goes for around 5,000,000 yen.

05:58.670 --> 06:00.490
All right, guys, let's work.

06:00.490 --> 06:01.720
You too, Lud-kun?

06:01.720 --> 06:04.440
You say that like it's entirely my fault.

06:04.440 --> 06:06.340
It is entirely <i>your</i> fault.

06:06.680 --> 06:07.950
That's true.

06:09.240 --> 06:11.080
Don't "a ha ha" me.

06:11.080 --> 06:13.260
You've been acting like an idiot all day.

06:13.260 --> 06:14.550
My tummy hurts!

06:14.550 --> 06:16.140
I can't stop farting!

06:16.140 --> 06:18.530
And what's up with that?

06:18.530 --> 06:20.870
Why do you fart whenever you
think something's funny?

06:20.870 --> 06:22.820
Do you have any remorse at all?

06:23.490 --> 06:24.650
Remorse?

06:24.650 --> 06:26.000
What's remorse?

06:28.570 --> 06:29.450
Motes,

06:30.800 --> 06:33.940
you're banned from doing those
kinds of pranks ever again.

06:33.940 --> 06:34.780
Got it?

06:35.260 --> 06:36.790
That's no fun.

06:36.790 --> 06:38.410
If you do, you don't get to eat.

06:40.440 --> 06:42.220
Oh, you and your jokes.

06:42.220 --> 06:43.110
I'm serious.

06:44.200 --> 06:47.670
Motes, you're seriously bothering everyone.

06:54.260 --> 06:55.520
All right, fine.

06:55.520 --> 06:57.010
I got it.

06:57.010 --> 07:00.350
I'll go easy on the pranks from now on.

07:00.630 --> 07:02.230
No one said to "go easy" on the pranks.

07:02.230 --> 07:03.590
Don't <i>do</i> them.

07:03.590 --> 07:05.600
Once every three days or so?

07:05.600 --> 07:06.600
I said no.

07:06.600 --> 07:07.960
Once every other week?

07:07.960 --> 07:08.990
I said no!

07:09.630 --> 07:11.280
Promise, all right?

07:11.280 --> 07:13.070
If you break the promise,
you don't get to eat.

07:14.150 --> 07:15.380
Got it?

07:20.030 --> 07:21.830
Answer her.

07:22.440 --> 07:24.000
Hello.

07:24.560 --> 07:26.090
Whoa, okonomiyaki.

07:26.090 --> 07:27.590
Nice.

07:27.590 --> 07:29.260
Help us out, Sousuke.

07:29.260 --> 07:30.300
Okay.

07:31.300 --> 07:32.960
What are you doing there, Motes-san?

07:34.980 --> 07:37.270
Well, well, if it isn't Sousuke-kun.

07:37.270 --> 07:38.370
Good evening.

07:39.460 --> 07:41.680
I've been reborn.

07:41.680 --> 07:46.330
I have succeeded in tucking away pranks

07:46.330 --> 07:49.570
such as kancho, knee jabs, and pit traps.

07:50.350 --> 07:51.070
Huh?

07:51.590 --> 07:54.910
From now on, I shall nurture in
myself an upstanding personality

07:54.910 --> 07:59.950
and live my life as a good adult,
earning my meals each day.

08:01.490 --> 08:02.220
Huh?

08:24.170 --> 08:25.180
I can't do it!

08:25.180 --> 08:27.440
I'm so bored, I'm going out of my mind!

08:27.700 --> 08:28.140
What?

08:28.140 --> 08:28.850
Why?

08:28.850 --> 08:30.880
Why are you getting ready for
dinner like there's nothing wrong?

08:30.880 --> 08:33.450
We're about to throw an okonomiyaki party.

08:32.560 --> 08:34.550
Who says they're going to
throw an okonomiyaki party

08:34.550 --> 08:37.610
and then goes ahead and makes okonomiyaki?

08:37.610 --> 08:39.160
I can't figure out what you're angry about.

08:39.160 --> 08:42.120
There's so many ways you
could make it more fun.

08:42.430 --> 08:43.870
Like doing this with the spatulas.

08:43.870 --> 08:45.170
Aonori

08:43.870 --> 08:45.170
Doing this with aonori.

08:45.410 --> 08:46.460
Doing this with the sauce.

08:46.690 --> 08:49.000
And why wouldn't you fry
the okonomiyaki like this?

08:49.390 --> 08:50.510
Come on, guys.

08:50.510 --> 08:51.840
Let's have some fun.

08:52.160 --> 08:54.970
We're all here, after all.

08:54.970 --> 08:55.980
Right?

08:58.970 --> 09:01.720
No one appreciates it.

09:01.720 --> 09:02.890
You're kidding me.

09:03.080 --> 09:04.570
That's enough.

09:04.570 --> 09:06.900
You haven't forgotten our promise, have you?

09:07.360 --> 09:10.620
The next time you do something,
you don't get to eat.

09:13.030 --> 09:15.600
Hey, is it my fault?

09:16.250 --> 09:17.950
Am I in the wrong?

09:18.800 --> 09:22.030
What do you think, Grandma?

09:22.760 --> 09:24.960
We totally don't know
each other, but tell me.

09:25.800 --> 09:28.840
I really think we should have more fun.

09:29.220 --> 09:31.390
What? I know, right?

09:31.390 --> 09:33.060
It's better to make things
more interesting, right?

09:33.060 --> 09:34.730
What fun is there in saying

09:34.730 --> 09:37.770
you're going to make okonomiyaki,
and then just plain making it, right?

09:37.770 --> 09:41.180
But I promised Kanae
I wouldn't pull any more pranks?

09:42.250 --> 09:43.870
That's true.

09:43.870 --> 09:46.200
I don't like breaking promises, either.

09:46.200 --> 09:48.650
It's not fun.

09:52.000 --> 09:53.350
All right.

09:53.350 --> 09:55.800
I'll hold on for a little longer.

09:55.800 --> 10:00.370
I'll try my best to enjoy this
terrible, no prank state of affairs.

10:01.230 --> 10:02.640
See you, Grandma.

10:02.640 --> 10:04.240
Not that we know each other at all.

10:04.720 --> 10:05.780
Thanks.

10:07.770 --> 10:09.720
Right as I'm saying that...

10:09.720 --> 10:11.500
Dude, are you serious?

10:11.890 --> 10:15.870
Damn it, Schu-kun. Your backside
is beckoning me to prank you.

10:15.870 --> 10:16.650
A trap?

10:16.650 --> 10:17.510
This isn't fair!

10:17.900 --> 10:21.280
Who wouldn't<i> push you in this situation?</i>

10:21.280 --> 10:22.890
No, no, no, what am I doing?

10:22.890 --> 10:24.120
I tried to push him just now.

10:24.120 --> 10:25.490
Man, I'm scary.

10:25.490 --> 10:27.650
You promised not to do it anymore, Motes.

10:27.650 --> 10:29.890
You're going to lose your next meal.

10:30.800 --> 10:31.610
But...

10:31.960 --> 10:33.570
It'll be fun.

10:33.840 --> 10:35.280
No, damn it!

10:35.280 --> 10:36.530
Fight it, Motes.

10:36.530 --> 10:37.390
Don't push him in.

10:37.390 --> 10:38.410
Don't push him in.

10:38.410 --> 10:39.350
Don't push him in.

10:39.350 --> 10:42.320
Don't push him in. Don't push
him in. Don't push him in.

10:42.320 --> 10:44.590
Don't push him in, Motes!

10:46.170 --> 10:47.540
B-But...

10:47.540 --> 10:49.840
But...

10:49.840 --> 10:51.580
Bam!

10:54.430 --> 10:56.120
I did it again.

10:56.120 --> 10:57.700
Schu-kun, you idiot!

10:57.700 --> 10:58.610
What?!

11:07.570 --> 11:11.210
Motes, you don't need to
get so depressed about it.

11:11.210 --> 11:12.770
Come have okonomiyaki with us.

11:13.080 --> 11:15.520
We aren't really that angry.

11:15.520 --> 11:16.990
It's not good for you.

11:16.990 --> 11:17.900
I forgive you.

11:17.900 --> 11:19.500
Get over here, Wolf.

11:19.500 --> 11:21.170
My masterpiece is getting cold.

11:21.170 --> 11:24.780
Shouldn't you all be worried about me?

11:26.640 --> 11:29.410
Tell him to cheer up, Schu-san.

11:29.410 --> 11:30.750
No way!

11:31.250 --> 11:32.710
Where are you going, Motes?

11:33.490 --> 11:34.630
For a walk.

11:36.470 --> 11:38.130
I'm bored.

11:38.550 --> 11:41.090
It's not fun being with you guys.

11:44.950 --> 11:45.930
Did he just lash out at us?

11:45.930 --> 11:47.380
What's his problem?

11:46.620 --> 11:47.850
That's who he is.

11:47.850 --> 11:48.800
I said I forgive him.

11:48.800 --> 11:50.720
How could he not be drawn to my masterpiece?

12:03.540 --> 12:04.440
Motes.

12:04.440 --> 12:06.000
Want to come shopping with me?

12:11.350 --> 12:12.800
Welcome home.

12:12.800 --> 12:14.220
You're home late.

12:15.470 --> 12:16.490
Motes.

12:16.490 --> 12:17.840
Dinner time.

12:18.330 --> 12:20.340
Where are you going, Motes?

12:20.800 --> 12:22.380
Motes.

12:31.670 --> 12:33.930
Motes is home late again.

12:34.350 --> 12:36.020
Oh, it's fine.

12:36.020 --> 12:38.830
I don't think we should
worry about it too much.

12:38.830 --> 12:40.230
He's always been like that.

12:40.590 --> 12:41.960
He's, like, moody.

12:41.960 --> 12:43.360
Temperamental.

12:43.630 --> 12:46.910
No, I think there's something
very suspicious about this.

12:47.230 --> 12:49.290
He doesn't tell us where he's
going. He comes home late.

12:49.290 --> 12:51.630
He's obviously avoiding us.

12:51.630 --> 12:54.580
He's definitely involved
in some kind of crime.

12:54.770 --> 12:55.870
C-Crime?

12:55.870 --> 12:57.840
Come on, Schu-san, you're overreacting.

12:58.230 --> 13:01.270
No, with that demon, it's possible.

13:01.270 --> 13:03.920
Have you forgotten about
the Hamagon incident?

13:04.180 --> 13:05.050
Hamagon?

13:05.760 --> 13:07.510
Oh, I remember that.

13:07.510 --> 13:08.970
His random awakening.

13:09.320 --> 13:12.430
He's no doubt being a massive nuisance.

13:14.260 --> 13:15.760
Why are you making that face?

13:17.900 --> 13:19.080
Motes.

13:19.940 --> 13:22.110
What have you been doing all this time?

13:23.180 --> 13:24.670
Let's see...

13:25.020 --> 13:25.970
Strolling?

13:25.970 --> 13:27.400
What?

13:27.400 --> 13:28.490
What about dinner?

13:28.490 --> 13:29.900
No, thanks.

13:31.230 --> 13:33.190
Way too suspicious.

13:33.190 --> 13:34.470
It's definitely crime.

13:34.470 --> 13:36.360
Trust me, it's not.

13:48.110 --> 13:49.730
Yo, what are we doing here?

13:49.730 --> 13:50.450
Shh!

13:50.450 --> 13:54.810
My little kitten, is it true that there's an
underground organization giving him money?

13:54.810 --> 13:55.420
What?

13:55.420 --> 13:59.230
Girl, is it true that Wolf has
re-awoken as the true Hamagon,

13:59.230 --> 14:03.330
and is going around town
violating all kinds of animals?

14:03.330 --> 14:04.930
How the hell did you come to that?!

14:04.930 --> 14:06.540
It's scary because it's plausible.

14:06.540 --> 14:07.750
Schu-san!

14:07.750 --> 14:08.780
Let's go home.

14:08.780 --> 14:09.850
Here we go.

14:11.540 --> 14:13.790
See, that's so suspicious.

14:14.150 --> 14:15.330
Uh...

14:15.330 --> 14:17.160
Is "suspicious" the right word?

14:17.430 --> 14:17.930
See?

14:17.930 --> 14:19.640
It's some kind of sign.

14:19.640 --> 14:21.840
I think he's walking
on just the white lines.

14:30.350 --> 14:31.700
Let's just leave him.

14:31.700 --> 14:33.300
Trust me, this doesn't mean anything.

14:33.300 --> 14:34.210
Let's go home.

14:34.210 --> 14:35.180
Impossible.

14:35.180 --> 14:37.350
He's going to make contact
with underground agents.

14:37.540 --> 14:40.010
That's not going to happen.

14:40.010 --> 14:40.820
Later.

14:43.500 --> 14:45.100
Sousuke, are you all right?

14:45.100 --> 14:47.300
I-It's a banana peel.

14:47.300 --> 14:48.570
A banana peel?

14:49.220 --> 14:51.600
Seriously? That's like
something out of an old gag.

14:51.600 --> 14:52.550
Jeez.

14:52.550 --> 14:53.490
Could it be...

14:58.530 --> 15:00.310
Cho-chan, look out!

15:01.230 --> 15:02.840
A-Are you okay?

15:03.200 --> 15:05.120
It's definitely happening.

15:05.120 --> 15:07.950
His Motes Panic has activated.

15:07.950 --> 15:08.760
Let's go home.

15:08.960 --> 15:10.670
Motes Panic?

15:11.060 --> 15:12.400
What's that?

15:12.400 --> 15:13.970
Allow me to explain.

15:14.440 --> 15:15.680
You know, Pad-kun?

15:15.910 --> 15:19.440
Motes Panic: an unavoidable nightmare.

15:19.800 --> 15:21.930
He doesn't do anything directly,

15:21.930 --> 15:25.420
but the powerful troublemaker
aura emanating from him

15:25.420 --> 15:29.670
brings calamity spontaneously
upon the people around him.

15:29.670 --> 15:35.950
It's as powerful and devastating as ten
snotty brats impervious to being scolded.

15:35.950 --> 15:36.800
Following him?

15:36.800 --> 15:38.410
Feel free to.

15:38.410 --> 15:40.460
I just hope you don't get hurt.

15:42.470 --> 15:44.080
Why do you even know that?

15:44.740 --> 15:46.250
And why do you look so happy?

15:46.910 --> 15:49.300
You be careful, too, Sousuke.

15:50.750 --> 15:51.610
Oh, my God!

15:51.610 --> 15:52.680
You freaking piece of shit!

15:52.680 --> 15:53.830
You little wretch!

15:54.610 --> 15:56.320
That's nonsense.

15:56.320 --> 15:58.310
Spontaneous calamities?

15:58.560 --> 16:01.340
That only happens in manga, not in...

16:01.630 --> 16:03.530
reality!

16:04.330 --> 16:06.820
Senpai!

16:07.570 --> 16:08.580
Let's go home.

16:19.480 --> 16:22.140
How are we supposed to survive?

16:22.140 --> 16:24.080
Beware the Motes Panic.

16:24.080 --> 16:25.170
Defeat.

16:25.170 --> 16:26.380
Let's go home.

16:26.840 --> 16:28.540
G-Guys...

16:29.180 --> 16:30.580
Get up, Landlady.

16:31.820 --> 16:33.180
We're going to lose him.

16:33.620 --> 16:35.330
I can't. I can't go on.

16:35.330 --> 16:36.760
You can't give up.

16:37.100 --> 16:38.620
We have to go after him.

16:38.620 --> 16:41.310
We must witness the truth with our own eyes.

16:41.710 --> 16:42.860
Schu-san...

16:43.400 --> 16:45.900
Now, let us go.

16:46.840 --> 16:48.020
Shoot!

16:48.280 --> 16:51.090
Mozart!

16:51.830 --> 16:54.730
Schu-san!

17:03.030 --> 17:05.450
I won't give up.

17:06.200 --> 17:09.820
I don't really remember how this happened,

17:10.360 --> 17:13.800
but just watch me.

18:19.530 --> 18:20.540
He's good.

18:20.970 --> 18:22.720
And he's an elementary school student.

18:23.790 --> 18:25.200
He's big, huh?

18:25.580 --> 18:28.680
That boy's always by himself.

18:29.160 --> 18:33.480
He used to play with his friends,
but now he comes by himself,

18:33.480 --> 18:36.550
plays by himself, and goes home by himself.

18:38.340 --> 18:41.930
I love watching him.

18:45.680 --> 18:48.600
Motes, did something happen?

18:50.250 --> 18:51.890
Lately, you've been—

18:51.890 --> 18:52.650
Time to go home.

18:56.850 --> 18:58.400
I'm getting hungry.

19:05.840 --> 19:07.210
Okay, see you then.

19:08.280 --> 19:10.220
I'm going this way.

19:11.520 --> 19:12.780
Where are you going?

19:16.210 --> 19:18.260
Well...

19:19.790 --> 19:21.220
To see my lover.

19:21.220 --> 19:22.180
Your lover?

19:22.490 --> 19:23.500
Yeah.

19:23.500 --> 19:25.750
I'm going to see my lover of seventeen.

19:25.750 --> 19:27.720
S-Seventeen?

19:29.000 --> 19:30.440
Wait, Motes.

19:33.340 --> 19:35.860
You're coming home, right?

19:38.670 --> 19:40.450
You're coming home, right?

19:51.480 --> 19:52.640
Seriously?!

19:52.640 --> 19:54.250
Seventeen? Is that okay?

19:54.250 --> 19:55.520
See? Crime.

19:55.520 --> 19:56.610
See?

19:56.610 --> 19:58.660
He never fails to surprise.

19:58.660 --> 20:00.270
I pray you hook up.

20:00.270 --> 20:01.880
I pray you get away with it.

20:04.190 --> 20:05.720
That Wolf.

20:06.250 --> 20:08.700
A seventeen-year-old lover, huh?

20:34.170 --> 20:36.670
Wolfgang Amadeus Mozart

20:38.670 --> 20:41.170
Symphony No. 25 in G Minor - K. 183

20:44.180 --> 20:46.930
A piece beloved
200 years after
its completion

20:50.680 --> 20:52.310
Mozart...

20:53.810 --> 20:56.060
...wrote it at seventeen.

21:15.360 --> 21:17.760
Too many dreams

21:17.760 --> 21:20.590
To carry in my two arms

21:20.590 --> 21:25.340
Just use your own head to overcome

21:25.340 --> 21:30.470
Don't mind the people who don't get it

21:30.470 --> 21:36.520
Make something of the
raging winds, if you must

21:36.520 --> 21:39.180
There's nothing to fear

21:39.180 --> 21:43.910
Don't be afraid of the future
or of a few obstacles

21:43.910 --> 21:47.060
You're going to capture your own future

21:49.150 --> 21:52.160
You're going to capture your own future

22:04.920 --> 22:08.480
You're going to capture your own future

22:21.080 --> 22:22.490
See you later.

22:38.000 --> 22:40.500
To be continued

24:10.970 --> 24:24.860
Breakthrough

24:11.930 --> 24:14.320
The intolerable emptiness of my existence.

24:14.320 --> 24:15.280
What am I?

24:15.280 --> 24:16.660
Why am I here?

24:16.660 --> 24:18.470
Not to be noticed by anyone,
not to create any trouble...

24:18.470 --> 24:20.020
What's wrong with freedom?

24:20.020 --> 24:20.980
You avocado!

24:20.980 --> 24:22.680
You aren't worthy of speaking about freedom.

24:22.680 --> 24:26.360
You salad, hamburger, and
sushi-transforming freak, bastard avocado!

24:26.360 --> 24:29.070
Oh, the loneliness of being an invisible man.
